# Day 12 - Salesforce DX & GitHub Workflow

## 🚀 What is Salesforce DX?
Salesforce DX (Developer Experience) is a modern development approach for Salesforce that focuses on:
- Source-driven development
- Version control integration
- Team collaboration
- Automation and CI/CD workflows

It helps developers build, test, and deploy Salesforce applications more efficiently.

---

## 💻 Why CLI Matters
Salesforce CLI (Command Line Interface) improves developer productivity by allowing:
- Faster project setup
- Easy deployment and retrieval of metadata
- Automation of repetitive tasks
- Integration with CI/CD pipelines

CLI makes development faster compared to manual UI-based work.

---

## 🔗 Why GitHub Matters
GitHub is essential for:
- Version control
- Tracking code changes
- Collaboration between developers
- Backup and history of code

It ensures every team member works on the same source code safely.

---

## 👥 Team Collaboration Problems
Without proper tools like DX + GitHub:
- Code conflicts occur frequently
- Hard to track changes
- Multiple developers overwrite each other’s work
- Deployment becomes risky and inconsistent

Salesforce DX + GitHub solves these issues using source control and structured workflows.

---

## 🏢 Enterprise Workflow Discussion
In enterprise environments:
- Developers use Salesforce DX for development
- GitHub manages version control
- CI/CD pipelines automate deployment
- Sandboxes are used for testing
- Production deployments are controlled and safe

This ensures scalable and reliable development.

---

